{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices","id":1052153,"title":"Cyborg Enforcers...Advices?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-20T13:30:24-08:00","id":1052153,"title":"Cyborg Enforcers...Advices?","content":"So, my players are fighting a technocratian amalgam which is pretty much The Iluminati.<br /> they are used to fight &quot;Men in black.&quot; but...i fucking love Cyborg 009 and i been fiddling with the idea of full infiltration units of cyborgs...but i dont have much experience with running technocracy or with the countermagick of primium ... or to make them even appear or show off as if they were &quot;Human Mages&quot; or &quot;traditional mages.&quot; any advices on how to run em? my players are arete 4-5 and i want to give them something that's an actual threat something to keep them worried about","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T15:36:49-08:00","id":1052233,"title":"","content":"Firstly, Primium countermeasures are expensive. And given the enhancements background only covers so much in the way of devices...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T15:59:26-08:00","id":1052244,"title":"","content":"hurmm..how would technocracian countermagick work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T16:10:32-08:00","id":1052250,"title":"","content":"Well. I'm not saying DON'T get it. Because it's a cyborgs only real defense against that nasty life three curse that basically just instagibs them.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is you should be careful about how much of it you give them. Generally speaking, I've found Mage heavily advantages the attacker.<br /> <br /> You get a maximum of 15 points of cybernetics through the enhancements background. 4 points of countermagick from Primium costs 8. That's over HALF of your points.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, you could give them a Martinez Robust hardsuit that they can take on and off as needed. And do the same exact thing for the same price, and leave your cybernetics points for actual cybernetics that do cool things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T16:14:57-08:00","id":1052252,"title":"","content":"I prefer the &quot;upgrades&quot; out of the progenitors book myself, everyone expects a cyborg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T16:30:53-08:00","id":1052260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1052252#post1052252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prefer the &quot;upgrades&quot; out of the progenitors book myself, everyone expects a cyborg.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could have both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T23:42:24-08:00","id":1052414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1052260#post1052260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could have both.</div> </div> </div> </div>But would your syndicate provided health care plan pay for both?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T01:10:53-08:00","id":1052444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1052414#post1052414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But would your syndicate provided health care plan pay for both?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you wouldn't have each person have both cybernetics and bio-augments, obviously. The team would be assembled from the ranks of both Iteration X and the Progenitors (probably Damage Control). Each member would have their own health care arrangements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T01:23:57-08:00","id":1052450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1052444#post1052444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you wouldn't have each person have both cybernetics and bio-augments, obviously. The team would be assembled from the ranks of both Iteration X and the Progenitors (probably Damage Control). Each member would have their own health care arrangements.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we both over thought each others statements \ud83d\ude09. I thought yours applied to the same npc, ergo taking both cyber and bio mods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T03:19:16-08:00","id":1052479,"title":"","content":"NPCs can have more than 5 points in enhancements. Even PCs can, it's just not <i>recommended</i> to allow it at character creation. This background can be bought several times.<br /> <br /> Just remember, each dot on this background gives 1 permadox or 1 genetic flaw (at least one permadox must be taken for cibernetics). <br /> <br /> Each dot can give +1 atribute or 3 points in devices (artifacts/talismans). <br /> <br /> Do you wanna some badass borgs?<br /> <br /> 4-5 Primium countermeasure, Wolverine Primium claws, cuz Primium have the extra advantage of negating magical soak (so, each success in your 4-5 Primium rate will remove one dice from vampiric Fortitude, werewolf/other fera Vigor, others) to soak your attack. Plus, Primium do aggravated damage (there's no claws like Primium claws). Give him a Bionic eye with a few perks (choose 3-5 or more if you wish, always on or switched at will sensorial magik from any sphere 1). Give him a plasma Cannon with 4-5 dices (damage of Forces, successes x2 plus 1), and that's it, at least for a &quot;Basic&quot; un-enlightened one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 02-21-2017, 06:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T06:46:51-08:00","id":1052538,"title":"","content":"If you have genegineering, you can't have devices and vice versa. So if you want bonuses you need to take the device that gives them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T00:30:01-08:00","id":1056007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1052244#post1052244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hurmm..how would technocracian countermagick work?</div> </div> </div> </div>-Setting the situation so that the caster's Paradigm is somehow put into doubt or shown to not be so universal. This can be done with a few well placed words or sentences.<br /> -Expressing scientific skepticism.<br /> -Mockery, laughing, being relaxed, showing no fear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T00:47:14-08:00","id":1056012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056007#post1056007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Setting the situation so that the caster's Paradigm is somehow put into doubt or shown to not be so universal. This can be done with a few well placed words or sentences.<br /> -Expressing scientific skepticism.<br /> -Mockery, laughing, being relaxed, showing no fear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or an <a href=\"https://youtu.be/FTKRoBjjyeI\" target=\"_blank\">Anti-magic Field Generator</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T00:56:16-08:00","id":1056014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056012#post1056012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or an <a href=\"https://youtu.be/FTKRoBjjyeI\" target=\"_blank\">Anti-magic Field Generator</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is more in the vein of Iteration-X or the Void Engineers I'd say. While the NWO, and of course the Syndicate with their Coincidental charm, would use the ones I mentioned, I imagine. A question is - where the Progenitors would stand?<br /> <br /> And all of this applies to Unweaving as well; including against Sorcerer magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 02-28-2017, 04:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T01:20:46-08:00","id":1056019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056014#post1056014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is more in the vein of Iteration-X or Void Engineers I'd say. While the NWO, and of course the Syndicate with their Coincidental charm, would use the ones I mentioned, I imagine. A question is - where the Progenitors would stand?<br /> <br /> And all of this applies to Unweaving as well; including against Sorcerer magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Progenitors might have inoculated themselves against parascientific attacks through chemical therapy, a symbiotic strain of protective bacteria, or nanomachines (son). They may try to engage these protections by verbally reaffirming their immunity, or by whipping out an injection or skin spray. Or else they may have grafted a gland to their body, just beneath the skin, that releases a hormone into their bloodstream when pressure is applied to the area (something like on the back of the neck would be subtle enough to pass as an unremarkable gesture). Or they might start spouting technobabble, like the others might. Or they might have modified their brain to have psychic powers, and they bend that ability towards countering their aggressors.<br /> <br /> I can also see other Technocratic Conventions using modifications and external tools for countermagic. A brain implant could come equipped with &quot;anti-mind-virus software&quot; to repel psionic intrusion. Both NWO and Syndicate agents love their gadgets, so either might carry a pocket-sized harmonic disrupter, or an injector full of short-lived nanites or a chemical cocktail that looks like an insulin needle.<br /> <br /> Nonverbal actions could be used to reestablish an agent's control of the situation, and their being above superstitious nonsense. Adjusting sunglasses or a tie, tracing the outline of a concealed weapon or a wallet, smoothing back hair, or checking the time as if bored. All of these things help to reaffirm the Technocrat's superiority in the situation, and keep them calm and composed. After all, these superstitionist &quot;incantations&quot; or &quot;hexes&quot; are just mind games, right? At best, the backwards mystic is trying to inject subconscious programming into the agent's mind, and engage a weird sort of Nocebo effect. So long as the agent doesn't lose his cool, they are immune to such tricks. They might even be able to force the superstitionist's mind to swallow its own mind-virus, if the agent acts cool enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T03:48:05-08:00","id":1056042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1052538#post1052538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have genegineering, you can't have devices and vice versa. So if you want bonuses you need to take the device that gives them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that WW did this for some game balancing... <br /> <br /> BUT... <br /> <br /> First of all, each point in this background gives 1 flaw or PERMADOX... So, taking 5 points in this, giving your char 5 permadox... Is too damn crippling already...<br /> <br /> Secondly... Why that limitation? I mean, if you are playing a Hermetic, you could put your magikal rubi in your forehead, and let it there until it fuses with your fleash... And you could have some attribute increase toghether with that, even if you make it permanent.<br /> <br /> What's more, I WONT get permadox for increasing my atrributes, unless I move them beyond 5.<br /> <br /> But, using this background, I could increase Strenght from 3 to 5 and still get permadox or &quot;genetic flaw&quot;.<br /> <br /> And... Common, this background is too damn expensive, has too many set backs, and it's not THAT overpowered as the description... To me it always seemed like White Wolf were so afraid of this (oh my God, an improved Techie! Run to the hills!) that they made so many restrictions, when in fact, a beggining char would do a lot better using those points in Avatar and/or Arcanum, or if using freebie, buying another Sphere dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T07:55:44-08:00","id":1056112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056042#post1056042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And... Common, this background is too damn expensive, has too many set backs, and it's not THAT overpowered as the description... To me it always seemed like White Wolf were so afraid of this (oh my God, an improved Techie! Run to the hills!) that they made so many restrictions, when in fact, a beginning char would do a lot better using those points in Avatar and/or Arcanum, or if using freebie, buying another Sphere dot.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does seem you're better off boosting your attributes yourself with spheres.<br /> <br /> Was this made after revised though? I kinda agree that their cost is high but revised rules might explain things a bit. Unless I'm mistaken, if you're using the revised rules to boost your attributes with life 3, you'd be taking 3 paradox or maybe 4 if you're a technocrat because it's not normally possible for them to raise attributes above normal levels without spheres and I do recall something about the books (Guide to the technocracy maybe) being stricter against the technocracy with regards to what they can do coincidentally.<br /> <br /> Not that I disagree with your assessment. I'm more trying to figure out what the writers were thinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T11:01:23-08:00","id":1056214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056019#post1056019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Progenitors might have inoculated themselves against parascientific attacks through chemical therapy, a symbiotic strain of protective bacteria, or nanomachines (son). They may try to engage these protections by verbally reaffirming their immunity, or by whipping out an injection or skin spray. Or else they may have grafted a gland to their body, just beneath the skin, that releases a hormone into their bloodstream when pressure is applied to the area (something like on the back of the neck would be subtle enough to pass as an unremarkable gesture). Or they might start spouting technobabble, like the others might. Or they might have modified their brain to have psychic powers, and they bend that ability towards countering their aggressors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pharmacopoeists might have pills to counter each of the Spheres; while Genegineers and FACADE Engineers modify their bodies in advance.<br /> <br /> Also I don't think it should be called \u201cspouting technobabble\u201d - the way Technocracy are head and shoulders deep in their Paradigm(s), this 'technobabble' might just be right through and through.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056019#post1056019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can also see other Technocratic Conventions using modifications and external tools for countermagic. A brain implant could come equipped with &quot;anti-mind-virus software&quot; to repel psionic intrusion. Both NWO and Syndicate agents love their gadgets, so either might carry a pocket-sized harmonic disrupter, or an injector full of short-lived nanites or a chemical cocktail that looks like an insulin needle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, full-on technological counters are options some of the agents choose or can requisition, I imagine. (or it gets provided by them with a suggestion that they use it for a given situation)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056019#post1056019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nonverbal actions could be used to reestablish an agent's control of the situation, and their being above superstitious nonsense. Adjusting sunglasses or a tie, tracing the outline of a concealed weapon or a wallet, smoothing back hair, or checking the time as if bored. All of these things help to reaffirm the Technocrat's superiority in the situation, and keep them calm and composed. After all, these superstitionist &quot;incantations&quot; or &quot;hexes&quot; are just mind games, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lighting a cigarette could also work excellently to show relaxation or dominance in a situation(s). (Especially as an Amalgam, with Perfect Timing. Very impressive as Counterspelling or Unweaving when they do it while being in different locations.)<br /> <br /> One stance I can see Technocracy agents adapting is that they are quite certain on some level that it <i>is</i> just mind games. While at the same time being aware that them demeaning the Magick or magic is what neutralizes it.<br /> <br /> Another way I can see Counterspelling or Unweaving done is through messing with a Mage's foci or a Sorcerer's items. A well experienced White Suit could destroy the work of an entire group of Sorcerers by burning one item, taking another one into her or his pocket, and throwing the other ones across the room with the right timing and the right pattern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 03-20-2017, 10:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T11:22:39-08:00","id":1056235,"title":"","content":"Another way of Technocratic Counterspelling and/or Unweaving that just came to my mind: through jokes and talking it out among themselves. An Arete 6+ Syndic or member of the NWO could Unweave whole Rituals with their laughter and knowing smirks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T13:41:43-08:00","id":1056304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056042#post1056042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I understand that WW did this for some game balancing...<br /> <br /> BUT...<br /> <br /> First of all, each point in this background gives 1 flaw or PERMADOX... So, taking 5 points in this, giving your char 5 permadox... Is too damn crippling already...<br /> <br /> Secondly... Why that limitation? I mean, if you are playing a Hermetic, you could put your magikal rubi in your forehead, and let it there until it fuses with your fleash... And you could have some attribute increase toghether with that, even if you make it permanent.<br /> <br /> What's more, I WONT get permadox for increasing my atrributes, unless I move them beyond 5.<br /> <br /> But, using this background, I could increase Strenght from 3 to 5 and still get permadox or &quot;genetic flaw&quot;.<br /> <br /> And... Common, this background is too damn expensive, has too many set backs, and it's not THAT overpowered as the description... To me it always seemed like White Wolf were so afraid of this (oh my God, an improved Techie! Run to the hills!) that they made so many restrictions, when in fact, a beggining char would do a lot better using those points in Avatar and/or Arcanum, or if using freebie, buying another Sphere dot.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it was an attempt at game balance it was a very poor one.<br /> <br /> I always took it for a flavor thing / an attempt at letting people 'dip their toe' in the whole transhumanism schtick the Technocracy has going on without it becoming a defining character feature.<br /> <br /> People who just want a little transhumanism take Genegineering and the mostly fluffy genetic flaws.<br /> <br /> People who want to go full bore take Cybernetics/Biomods and take permadox.<br /> <br /> And given that you can get the SAME EXACT EFFECT as genegineering for 2 out of the 3 points of devices you get. (In some cases you can even get more, for example an added health level that let's you soak aggravated damage with your stamina.)<br /> <br /> Cybernetics has more to offer, but is also harsher on you. Genegineering is the light option.<br /> <br /> Also, you're not increasing your strength from '3 to 5' you're adding two to your strength.<br /> <br /> If you then use XP to increase your strength to 4, your strength would effectively be six. Etc Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T17:05:52-08:00","id":1056378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056304#post1056304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it was an attempt at game balance it was a very poor one.<br /> <br /> I always took it for a flavor thing / an attempt at letting people 'dip their toe' in the whole transhumanism schtick the Technocracy has going on without it becoming a defining character feature.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not flavor because it's not free... Actually, it has a HUGE cost, compared to other things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056304#post1056304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, you're not increasing your strength from '3 to 5' you're adding two to your strength.<br /> <br /> If you then use XP to increase your strength to 4, your strength would effectively be six. Etc Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet, if I bleed myself for 4 full moons while singing prayers to the godess with my Verbena, I can give myself a permanent increase of my strenght from 3 to 5 without getting myself some permadox.<br /> <br /> Besides, how is a Victor clone made? He would have to have 7+5+3 = 15 genetic flaws just to have the same as a beggining char, not to mention all the skills!!!<br /> <br /> That also makes the descriptions of very powerful unenlightened cyborgs very unreal or very silly. They'll either be too broken to be functional, or, since it could all be permadox, and since paradox has NO effects on unenlightned, those cyborgs could have up to 50 permadox without prejudice... And be some freaking mutants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T18:45:51-08:00","id":1056412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056378#post1056378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet, if I bleed myself for 4 full moons while singing prayers to the godess with my Verbena, I can give myself a permanent increase of my strenght from 3 to 5 without getting myself some permadox.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you WOULD suffer Pattern Bleeding, because you were twisting your body's pattern with a Life effect for longer than one day.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That also makes the descriptions of very powerful unenlightened cyborgs very unreal or very silly. They'll either be too broken to be functional, or, since it could all be permadox, and since paradox has NO effects on unenlightned, those cyborgs could have up to 50 permadox without prejudice... And be some freaking mutants. </div> </div> </div>At least according to M20, Permadox belonging to unAwakened characters would contribute to the Paradox of their nearest Awakened ally. It's blatant how that rule only exists to close a loophole, and doesn't make a lot of sense, but it's there.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, a Storyteller could rule that, since the cyborg is unAwakened, they don't have a Paradox pool, and thus their crime against the Consensus would need to be counterbalanced in some other fashion. Like Non-Genetic Genetic Flaws.<br /> <br /> Alternatively alternatively, because the Enhancements are effectively Devices (that have simply been installed inside the body), the Paradox would still accrue and backlash against their wielder in much the way a non-Enhancement Device or Talisman would in the hands of an unAwakened user. It's not like Paradox cares whether the Awakened Effect is used by a person with Arete or an item with Arete, so why should it care if that &quot;item&quot; were also part of a person's body?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T20:09:15-08:00","id":1056437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056412#post1056412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you WOULD suffer Pattern Bleeding, because you were twisting your body's pattern with a Life effect for longer than one day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even with Life 5? (That has always been my doubt).<br /> <br /> Besides, you can go around some Pattern Bleeding, a resourceful Mage (and I guess one Mage that can increase his attributes permanently would be resourceful) could have a steady supply of quintessence to balance that. Well, with a Periapt and an auto effect, he wouldn't even feel it (no pain, no nothing).<br /> <br /> You can't, however, go around &quot;genetic flaws&quot; or Permadox. So, it's not balanced (lets be honest, after a point, getting quintessence is trivial for most powerful Mages).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056412#post1056412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least according to M20, Permadox belonging to unAwakened characters would contribute to the Paradox of their nearest Awakened ally. It's blatant how that rule only exists to close a loophole, and doesn't make a lot of sense, but it's there.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, unenlightned cyborgs would never work along enlightened agents, unless under the most dire situations. And yeah, that rule sucks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056412#post1056412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, a Storyteller could rule that, since the cyborg is unAwakened, they don't have a Paradox pool, and thus their crime against the Consensus would need to be counterbalanced in some other fashion. Like Non-Genetic Genetic Flaws.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, those are good house rules. RAW however, sucks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056412#post1056412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively alternatively, because the Enhancements are effectively Devices (that have simply been installed inside the body), the Paradox would still accrue and backlash against their wielder in much the way a non-Enhancement Device or Talisman would in the hands of an unAwakened user. It's not like Paradox cares whether the Awakened Effect is used by a person with Arete or an item with Arete, so why should it care if that &amp;quot;item&amp;quot; were also part of a person's body?</div> </div> </div> </div>Invents (tech talismans, items with Arete and 1 will of it's maker) are very rare. And, in my opnion, those rules are good, but still flawed.<br /> Invents can work by their own but... How many Prime 5 Masters do the Union have that are <u>willing to sacrifice one permanent will point</u> just to give an operative a <i>really good</i> device, even more so when you consider that, should your beautiful cyborg 2.0 gets smashed and those RDs freakes lot his body, they'll have a piece of YOU... That's not something to take lightly.<br /> So, the VAST majority of the devices are NOT invents (talismans). They are <i>artifacts</i>. Items with magikal effects, but without an Arete rating, so, therefore, suposedly, only other awakened can use them, because the roll made will be the role of the wearer's Arete (since the item have no Arete of it's own).<br /> <br /> However...<br /> <br /> I just looked over Forged by Dragons' Fire. And it says that, artifacts can only be used by the Awakened or <u>Acolytes, Extraordinary Citizens, Sorcerors</u> (if it matches their Paradigm, which is fine).<br /> <br /> Ok, that's cool. I REALLY wouldn't expect all those unenlightened cyborgs and agents out there filled with several talismans... I really can't imagine all the Union's Masters devoided of their willpower because they need to keep wasting it on every single second class device that the lowest level agent could lay their hands on. So, if Extraordinary Citizens can use normal artifacts, the scenario makes sense once again.<br /> <br /> Except for one small detailed (which, of course, WW forgot to adress in the book)<br /> <br /> What do the Acolyte roll to use the item, since they DON'T have an Arete rating?<br /> <br /> Well, Sorcerors can &quot;do Magic&quot; without generating Paradox... So, besides that talk about what will the proletarian agent roll (WP? Very OP, since it's a lot easier to get willpower 8 than Arete 8), there is this thing about paradox. Sorcerors don't have paradox when they use their Magic... But would them generate it using artifacts?<br /> <br /> Talismans aren't a problem, they accumulate the paradox within the item and will simply break when they are full (that can be a problem for a cyborg with a quantum positronic brain that can do shit no human can... But can break if you abuse of it's RAM).<br /> <br /> So, the rules for the non-Mage to use those items are really lacking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T22:06:50-08:00","id":1056482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056437#post1056437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Invents (tech talismans, items with Arete and 1 will of it's maker) are very rare. And, in my opnion, those rules are good, but still flawed.<br /> Invents can work by their own but... How many Prime 5 Masters do the Union have that are <u>willing to sacrifice one permanent will point</u> just to give an operative a <i>really good</i> device, even more so when you consider that, should your beautiful cyborg 2.0 gets smashed and those RDs freakes lot his body, they'll have a piece of YOU... That's not something to take lightly.<br /> So, the VAST majority of the devices are NOT invents (talismans). They are <i>artifacts</i>. Items with magikal effects, but without an Arete rating, so, therefore, suposedly, only other awakened can use them, because the roll made will be the role of the wearer's Arete (since the item have no Arete of it's own).<br /> <br /> However...<br /> <br /> I just looked over Forged by Dragons' Fire. And it says that, artifacts can only be used by the Awakened or <u>Acolytes, Extraordinary Citizens, Sorcerors</u> (if it matches their Paradigm, which is fine).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to stop you right there, because you are mistaken. Artifacts cannot be used by anyone BUT a mage. I checked Forged By Dragon's Fire, and it confirms this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Forged By Dragon's Fire, p. 15-16</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Artifacts work by optimizing the <b>mage's own magical abilities</b>. An Artifact is like a rote and a focus all neatly bundled together and waiting for the <b>spark of the mage's Enlightenment</b>. When the mage triggers the Artifact, it is <b>the mage's own Arete</b> that is rolled...</div> </div> </div> </div>Talismans are the ones that can be used by Sleepers, because, as I stated, Talismans have their own Arete score.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Forged By Dragon's Fire, p. 46</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages...can loan <b>Talismans</b> to others - even Sleepers - <b>because they have their own Arete score</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you said that Acolytes, Extraordinary Citizens, and Sorcerers can use Artifacts, I checked. You are thinking of Charms and Gadgets, not Artifacts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Forged By Dragon's Fire, p. 26</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">One need not be Awakened to use <b>Charms or Gadgets</b>, but generally only consors and Acolytes ever do so. A Sleeper who believes in the magic's paradigm can trigger the magic in a <b>Charm</b> by spending a point of Willpower...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcerers and Extraordinary Citizens are capable of performing feats of Magic/Science because they are using their tools as Foci/Instruments of their Path-based effects, not because the equipment they use is inherently magical. The one exception to this is using the Path of Enchantment...which creates a Talisman, not an Artifact. (Just, you know, a simpler one).<br /> <br /> M20, meanwhile, is very clear that Enhancements are internal Devices, distinct from Instruments (though particular implants/mods can be used for both).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20 Core, p. 657</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As mentioned in the appropriate entries in Chapter Ten, simple cybernetics serve as instruments and practices for hypertech procedures. (See p. 576 and 579.) Thus, many characters employ minor cybernetic adjustments too subtle for the Enhancements Background.</div> </div> </div> </div>It goes on further to say that (cybernetic) Enhancements have &quot;Self-Contained Energy&quot; (Quintessence pools) and &quot;Activation&quot; (Enlightenment/Arete rating), emphatically excluding the possibility that they are anything but Devices/Talismans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 03-01-2017, 01:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T08:43:32-08:00","id":1056649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056437#post1056437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even with Life 5? (That has always been my doubt).<br /> <br /> Besides, you can go around some Pattern Bleeding, a resourceful Mage (and I guess one Mage that can increase his attributes permanently would be resourceful) could have a steady supply of quintessence to balance that. Well, with a Periapt and an auto effect, he wouldn't even feel it (no pain, no nothing).<br /> <br /> You can't, however, go around &amp;quot;genetic flaws&amp;quot; or Permadox. So, it's not balanced (lets be honest, after a point, getting quintessence is trivial for most powerful Mages).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, unenlightned cyborgs would never work along enlightened agents, unless under the most dire situations. And yeah, that rule sucks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yep, those are good house rules. RAW however, sucks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Invents (tech talismans, items with Arete and 1 will of it's maker) are very rare. And, in my opnion, those rules are good, but still flawed.<br /> Invents can work by their own but... How many Prime 5 Masters do the Union have that are <u>willing to sacrifice one permanent will point</u> just to give an operative a <i>really good</i> device, even more so when you consider that, should your beautiful cyborg 2.0 gets smashed and those RDs freakes lot his body, they'll have a piece of YOU... That's not something to take lightly.<br /> So, the VAST majority of the devices are NOT invents (talismans). They are <i>artifacts</i>. Items with magikal effects, but without an Arete rating, so, therefore, suposedly, only other awakened can use them, because the roll made will be the role of the wearer's Arete (since the item have no Arete of it's own).<br /> <br /> However...<br /> <br /> I just looked over Forged by Dragons' Fire. And it says that, artifacts can only be used by the Awakened or <u>Acolytes, Extraordinary Citizens, Sorcerors</u> (if it matches their Paradigm, which is fine).<br /> <br /> Ok, that's cool. I REALLY wouldn't expect all those unenlightened cyborgs and agents out there filled with several talismans... I really can't imagine all the Union's Masters devoided of their willpower because they need to keep wasting it on every single second class device that the lowest level agent could lay their hands on. So, if Extraordinary Citizens can use normal artifacts, the scenario makes sense once again.<br /> <br /> Except for one small detailed (which, of course, WW forgot to adress in the book)<br /> <br /> What do the Acolyte roll to use the item, since they DON'T have an Arete rating?<br /> <br /> Well, Sorcerors can &amp;quot;do Magic&amp;quot; without generating Paradox... So, besides that talk about what will the proletarian agent roll (WP? Very OP, since it's a lot easier to get willpower 8 than Arete 8), there is this thing about paradox. Sorcerors don't have paradox when they use their Magic... But would them generate it using artifacts?<br /> <br /> Talismans aren't a problem, they accumulate the paradox within the item and will simply break when they are full (that can be a problem for a cyborg with a quantum positronic brain that can do shit no human can... But can break if you abuse of it's RAM).<br /> <br /> So, the rules for the non-Mage to use those items are really lacking.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, no idea where you got the invents term from. But technomantic and hypertech devices don't require a point of willpower.<br /> <br /> Also, paradox caused by devices generally hits the device rather than the wielder. Though sometimes (usually thanks to the ST.) the weilder gets caught in the blast radius.<br /> <br /> The trade-off is that they also lack that connection to you and you can't use them to shatter the action economy over your knee.<br /> <br /> So yes every piece of gear that has an Arete score, is actually equivalent to a talisman.<br /> <br /> Secondly, constructs are either enlightened in their own right, or should possess the paradox vulnerability / soulless flaw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T12:29:06-08:00","id":1056731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056649#post1056649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OK, no idea where you got the invents term from.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont have the Forged by Dragon in english, only the version in portuguese. They translated it as &quot;Invent&quot;, the Technocratic version of Talisman.<br /> <br /> I dont remember the proper name in english<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056649#post1056649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But technomantic and hypertech devices don't require a point of willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it doesn't take a will pt, its NOT a Talisman, its an artifact, and doesn't have Arete of its own<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056649#post1056649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, paradox caused by devices generally hits the device rather than the wielder. Though sometimes (usually thanks to the ST.) the weilder gets caught in the blast radius.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, those are amonsgt the additional ways of dealing with Paradox (all done with Prime 5). Most of the times, the Wonder will suck up all the Paradox to itself (it may just break harmlessly beyond repair, or unleash all its quota in a single insane backlash)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056649#post1056649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The trade-off is that they also lack that connection to you and you can't use them to shatter the action economy over your knee.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't understand that<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056649#post1056649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yes every piece of gear that has an Arete score, is actually equivalent to a talisman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but for that, the maker must put a permanent point of willpower to attach his Arete score to the item<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056649#post1056649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly, constructs are either enlightened in their own right, or should possess the paradox vulnerability / soulless flaw.</div> </div> </div> </div>Souless? Can't a &quot;basic&quot; extraordinary citizen (a sleeper) have augments?<br /> Ok, needing the flaw Paradox vulnerability is a good one, at least for game balancing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T12:51:23-08:00","id":1056747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056482#post1056482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to stop you right there, because you are mistaken. Artifacts cannot be used by anyone BUT a mage. I checked Forged By Dragon's Fire, and it confirms this.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, my mistake.<br /> <br /> However, what about artifacts with always on fixed effects that dont require Arete rolls (like a tinfoil hat that grants a permanent 5 successes mental shield while weared)?<br /> <br /> The book wasn't very specific about that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056482#post1056482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talismans are the ones that can be used by Sleepers, because, as I stated, Talismans have their own Arete score.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056482#post1056482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you said that Acolytes, Extraordinary Citizens, and Sorcerers can use Artifacts, I checked. You are thinking of Charms and Gadgets, not Artifacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, thats actually an interesting thing. For example:<br /> <br /> Your plasma Cannon needs Power Cells to work. The Power Cells are useless after their charges are over.<br /> <br /> Power Cells could be disposable Gadgets... Use it, throw it away, get a new one (Power Cells are good for plasma, laser and Ion weapons, and for implanted cyber cannons too)<br /> <br /> Positronic Brains are great, but they need Quantum Processing Units. Sadly, those are highly unstable, and will break after use, soso you'll need a constant supply.<br /> <br /> So, the Enhancment background would have a &quot;maintenance&quot; with it (a special kind of back, which grants you a supply of the gadge YOU need to make your &quot;augments&quot; work... As long as you are good with the bureoucracy of the Union)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056482#post1056482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcerers and Extraordinary Citizens are capable of performing feats of Magic/Science because they are using their tools as Foci/Instruments of their Path-based effects, not because the equipment they use is inherently magical. The one exception to this is using the Path of Enchantment...which creates a Talisman, not an Artifact. (Just, you know, a simpler one).</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont think that ALL sleeper agents of the Union are Sorcerors with Paths. Or, at the very least, not all of them have the several Paths they would need for some of their stunts. They do, however, make use of Devices, nevertheless.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that some &quot;things&quot; the Union have are too dumb to have paths, but even so they are mountains of devices... Like Hit Marks (I dont think that those things are actually secretly &quot;sorcerors&quot;)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056482#post1056482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">M20, meanwhile, is very clear that Enhancements are internal Devices, distinct from Instruments (though particular implants/mods can be used for both).</div> </div> </div> </div>And what does that mean?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056482#post1056482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It goes on further to say that (cybernetic) Enhancements have &quot;Self-Contained Energy&quot; (Quintessence pools) and &quot;Activation&quot; (Enlightenment/Arete rating), emphatically excluding the possibility that they are anything but Devices/Talismans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, but now we have a SERiOUS problem. Because, thats a LOT of permanent willpower drained from the Masters of the Union.<br /> <br /> Its NOT just the borgs.<br /> <br /> The problem is: all those proletarians agents using those sunglasses devices. Its all the plasma weapons out there. Thats the real problem","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 03-01-2017, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T13:30:14-08:00","id":1056770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://umbral-domains.wikidot.com/cybernetics\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://d3g0gp89917ko0.cloudfront.net/v--291054f06006/common--images/social/twitter.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://umbral-domains.wikidot.com/cybernetics\" target=\"_blank\"> Of Metal and Spirit: A Piecemeal Dream - Umbral Domains </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://umbral-domains.wikidot.com/cybernetics\" target=\"_blank\"> http://umbral-domains.wikidot.com/cybernetics </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Here are some headcannon house rules for cybernetics. Its interesting, all try to seek some exerts of GURPS ultratech and similar and make some adjusts, it is by far the most detailed source about that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T14:48:35-08:00","id":1056806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056731#post1056731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont have the Forged by Dragon in english, only the version in portuguese. They translated it as &amp;quot;Invent&amp;quot;, the Technocratic version of Talisman.<br /> <br /> I dont remember the proper name in english<br /> <br /> <br /> If it doesn't take a will pt, its NOT a Talisman, its an artifact, and doesn't have Arete of its own<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, those are amonsgt the additional ways of dealing with Paradox (all done with Prime 5). Most of the times, the Wonder will suck up all the Paradox to itself (it may just break harmlessly beyond repair, or unleash all its quota in a single insane backlash)<br /> <br /> <br /> I didn't understand that<br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, but for that, the maker must put a permanent point of willpower to attach his Arete score to the item<br /> <br /> <br /> Souless? Can't a &amp;quot;basic&amp;quot; extraordinary citizen (a sleeper) have augments?<br /> Ok, needing the flaw Paradox vulnerability is a good one, at least for game balancing</div> </div> </div> </div>OK. The problem is the rules for technomantic devices are in technomancers toybox. Not forged by dragons fire.<br /> <br /> Normal talismans act on their own. They use that fragment of will to cast independently of the wielder. So you can use your wand of flight and cast a bolt of fire on the same turn.<br /> <br /> Devices don't do that. They are magic things with their own power, but lacking will of their own. They require the wielder to actively use them and essentially babysit them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T17:08:12-08:00","id":1056862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056806#post1056806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OK. The problem is the rules for technomantic devices are in technomancers toybox. Not forged by dragons fire.<br /> <br /> Normal talismans act on their own. They use that fragment of will to cast independently of the wielder. So you can use your wand of flight and cast a bolt of fire on the same turn.<br /> <br /> Devices don't do that. They are magic things with their own power, but lacking will of their own. They require the wielder to actively use them and essentially babysit them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... Ok. I never took the trouble of REALLY reading technomancers toybox, I found it rather boring, and I didn't knew of that new type of Wonder... Well, its cool, but it should also be present in dragons fire.<br /> <br /> Question: mystics can do it too right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T17:37:24-08:00","id":1056875,"title":"","content":"It's presented as a Technomancer only thing caused by the difference in paradigms. Details are on page Nine and Ten. But the way it's described I could see mystics of a certain sort making use of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T17:58:06-08:00","id":1056895,"title":"","content":"Oh, thats bullshit... Why do the techie can do those super freaking awesome things so easily that ANYONE could use but the mystics with centuries to thousands of years of experience can't? Oh no, thats not right.<br /> <br /> Besides, I dont like to simply veto stuff for one or another group just randomly<br /> <br /> (On the brighter side, its good to refresh my memory about the Union using industrial mass production for their devices, I wasn't wrong about it)<br /> <br /> Thats giving too much Power to the Technocracy (they already mass produce troops and toys).<br /> <br /> No no no, its oficial now, in my games now, both Trads and Techies can build items with Arete without the Willpower<br /> <br /> Harder rules, Im ok with, maybe those aren't as common with nystics because of reasons, but simply vetoing it... No","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T18:33:03-08:00","id":1056917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technomancer's Toybox page 10</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Unlike Talismans, Devices do not require the sacrifice of a Willpower point; they do, however, take twice the usual time to build unless there's some sort of assembly line on the Realm. Most Technocracy's Constructs do include mass production facilities - that's where they get those wonderful toys! - but most Sons of Ether and Virtual Adepts will prefer the personal touch&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh comon, thats bullshit<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...but most <b>Suckers</b> of Ether and Virtual <b>Inepts</b> will prefer the personal touch&quot; </div> </div> </div>Thats what happens when you leave the Union. You become stupid.<br /> <br /> Superstitious idiots","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 03-01-2017, 09:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T18:46:58-08:00","id":1056925,"title":"","content":"Yeah, looking through my copy of Technomancer's Toybox, it does seem kind of unfair that mystics need to invest permanent Willpower, but technomancers don't. I mean, there's a good reason for it (why should a scientist have to invest their Willpower to make a machine work, if they believe that the machine functions because of laws of science), and I agree with it. But it still unbalances things in the favor of technomancers...and when they already have so many things in their favor.<br /> <br /> So how do we fix that? One idea would be that, regardless of how well the creation process goes, Devices automatically come with at least one Flaw (with a value equal to its Arete/Enlightenment rating). Mystics had centuries - if not millennia - to perfect their methods, and the investment of permanent Willpower binds their Talismans together more tightly. Technomancers may have the advantage in that Reality is more lenient on them, but the &quot;laws&quot; the Devices are based on might not be wholly accepted, if at all. And such machine-magic is new, often experimental. Especially in the case of the Etherites and Virtual Adepts, their creations are liable to have faults that, try as they might, just refuse to smooth out. It's only when a Device has been refined enough that it enters into the Consensus (even if only for Hedge Scientists) that the bugs get worked out.<br /> <br /> This applies even to Technocrats. They aren't immune to the problems inherent to the prototype process. Their advantage is merely having enough resources that they can throw designs against the wall until they get one whose Flaws are...manageable. The hi-tech sunglasses the NWO agent sports, that feeds her streams of data, aren't perfect. They are just the sunglasses that have the least crippling faults. (Assuming the sunglasses are Devices, instead of just Instruments with no Enlightenment score of their own).<br /> <br /> That the idea of the &quot;state-of-the-art equipment&quot; being buggy and error-prone also helps feed into the Union's party line. If Paradox hits a Device and causes some spectacular backlash, the agent is liable to blame the lack of perfection in the designs, rather than some kind of omnipotent force of karmic balance, acting against the Technocrat for their hubris. The latter is superstitionist talk, and not worth considering further.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 03-02-2017, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T20:18:05-08:00","id":1056958,"title":"","content":"The Paradigm for technotoys is broken. Its not just technobabble pseudoscience, its totally broken.<br /> <br /> -&quot;Cool! I can see extra Dimensional beings with my kirlian sunglasses!&quot; (common Instrument - foci - without any magikal powers whatsoever. The agent simply uses Spirit 1, the sunglasses is just the focus to the effect, norhing more)<br /> -&quot;Oh, let me see that (his unenlightened friend asks his glasses)<br /> -&quot;Hum... I can't see a thing&quot;<br /> -&quot;Thats because you're dumb. You dont understand how to use the glasses&quot;<br /> -&quot;Sooo... I dont understand how to look throw the sunglasses?&quot;<br /> -&quot;Nevermind&quot;<br /> -&quot;By the way, why does your plasma gun only works when youre the one using it, or just when you're around?&quot;<br /> -&quot;Sights&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T21:32:44-08:00","id":1056971,"title":"","content":"Well the disadvantage is that devices count as the character casting, despite using the devices arete.<br /> <br /> I have two Plasma guns. I can only shoot one at a time. Because you can only perform one act of magic a turn.<br /> <br /> You have two rings of plasma bolt summoning. You can fire off two bolts of plasma and then perform a spell of your own. Because your rings have their own will and actions. Of course all it can do with those actions is cast spells. Because it's a ring. But whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T08:38:29-08:00","id":1057106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052153-cyborg-enforcers-advices?p=1056958#post1056958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Paradigm for technotoys is broken. Its not just technobabble pseudoscience, its totally broken.<br /> <br /> -&quot;Cool! I can see extra Dimensional beings with my kirlian sunglasses!&quot; (common Instrument - foci - without any magikal powers whatsoever. The agent simply uses Spirit 1, the sunglasses is just the focus to the effect, norhing more)<br /> -&quot;Oh, let me see that (his unenlightened friend asks his glasses)<br /> -&quot;Hum... I can't see a thing&quot;<br /> -&quot;Thats because you're dumb. You dont understand how to use the glasses&quot;<br /> -&quot;Sooo... I dont understand how to look throw the sunglasses?&quot;<br /> -&quot;Nevermind&quot;<br /> -&quot;By the way, why does your plasma gun only works when youre the one using it, or just when you're around?&quot;<br /> -&quot;Sights&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds almost like what happened in BBC one's Sherlock (Season 3 Episode 3) with Sherlock and Charles Augustus Magnussen.<br /> <br /> But more actually related, I always thought that the tech would be using items that actually showed them something but that didn't didn't make sense to anyone untrained but could be replicated with cutting edge technology. Like shades that show a bunch of numbers and colors that are impossible for a normal person to interpret or a plasma that has to be set to take things like humidity, range, electromagnetic interference, and other factors or else you get an explosion, a fire, or something like a circuit-breaker shut down (or something). Then I imagined that the items anyone can use are made with willpower taken from some poor unfortunates the technocracy has access to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T06:02:17-08:00","id":1057558,"title":"","content":"@Spacecat<br /> Some poor <b>awakened</b> unfortunate.<br /> <br /> But that is a nice way for Technocrats to get extra credit. The Technocrats way of infernalism...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}